# MyAI PDF Browser - Electron Application Rules

## Project Overview

This is an Electron-based desktop application that combines PDF viewing/editing with web browsing capabilities, featuring an AI assistant. The app uses Chromium's BrowserView to provide true embedded browser functionality without iframe restrictions.

## Architecture & Tech Stack

### Core Technologies

- **Frontend**: React + TypeScript + Vite
- **Backend**: Electron (Node.js)
- **Rendering Engine**: Chromium (via Electron BrowserView)
- **PDF Processing**: pdfjs-dist + pdf-lib
- **AI Integration**: OpenAI API
- **UI Framework**: Radix UI Icons + Custom CSS

### Key Directories

- `/frontend/src/` - React frontend code
- `/main.js` - Electron main process
- `/preload.js` - IPC communication bridge
- `/frontend/build/` - Production build output

## Development Rules

### 1. Electron-Specific Guidelines

#### Main Process (`main.js`)

- **Window Management**: Handle main window creation and lifecycle
- **BrowserView**: Create and manage embedded browser functionality
- **IPC Handlers**: All backend functionality via ipcMain.handle()
- **Security**: Configure web security bypass for browser view
- **File Operations**: Use Node.js fs module for file handling

#### Renderer Process (React Frontend)

```typescript
// Always use Electron APIs via preload bridge
const result = await window.electronAPI.navigateUrl(url);

// Handle async operations with proper error handling
try {
  const fileData = await window.electronAPI.openFileDialog();
} catch (error) {
  console.error("File operation failed:", error);
}
```

#### IPC Communication Pattern

```javascript
// Main process (main.js)
ipcMain.handle("operation-name", async (event, params) => {
  try {
    // Perform operation
    return { success: true, data: result };
  } catch (error) {
    return { success: false, error: error.message };
  }
});

// Preload (preload.js)
contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld("electronAPI", {
  operationName: (params) => ipcRenderer.invoke("operation-name", params),
});

// Renderer (React)
const result = await window.electronAPI.operationName(params);
```

### 2. BrowserView Implementation

#### Creating Embedded Browser

```javascript
const browserView = new BrowserView({
  webPreferences: {
    nodeIntegration: false,
    contextIsolation: true,
    webSecurity: false, // Bypass iframe restrictions
    allowRunningInsecureContent: true,
  },
});

// Position within main window
browserView.setBounds({ x: 50, y: 200, width: 1000, height: 600 });
```

#### Security Bypass for Restricted Sites

```javascript
browserView.webContents.session.webRequest.onHeadersReceived(
  (details, callback) => {
    // Remove headers that prevent embedding
    delete details.responseHeaders["x-frame-options"];
    delete details.responseHeaders["X-Frame-Options"];
    delete details.responseHeaders["content-security-policy"];
    delete details.responseHeaders["Content-Security-Policy"];

    callback({ responseHeaders: details.responseHeaders });
  }
);
```

### 3. Frontend Development Rules

#### React Component Structure

```typescript
// Type definitions for Electron APIs
declare global {
  interface Window {
    electronAPI: {
      navigateUrl: (url: string) => Promise<{ success: boolean }>;
      // ... other APIs
    };
  }
}

// Component with Electron integration
function BrowserComponent() {
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!window.electronAPI) return;

    window.electronAPI.onBrowserLoading((data) => {
      setIsLoading(data.loading);
    });

    return () => {
      window.electronAPI.removeAllListeners("browser-loading");
    };
  }, []);
}
```

#### State Management

- **Tabs**: Use `tabs` state array with `activeId` for tab management
- **PDF State**: Store `pdfBytes`, `fileName`, `filePath`, `pageNum` per tab
- **Browser State**: Use `currentUrl`, `isWebView`, `omniboxValue`
- **Debug**: Use `addDebugLog()` for user-visible debugging

### 4. PDF Functionality Rules

#### PDF Loading via Electron

```typescript
// Use Electron file dialog
const fileResult = await window.electronAPI.openFileDialog();
if (fileResult.success && fileResult.data) {
  const pdfBytes = new Uint8Array(fileResult.data);
  await renderPDFPage(pdfBytes, 1);
}
```

#### PDF Rendering

```typescript
// Configure pdfjs-dist worker
useEffect(() => {
  pdfjsLib.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = `//cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/pdf.js/${pdfjsLib.version}/pdf.worker.min.js`;
}, []);

// Render PDF page
async function renderPDFPage(pdfBytes: Uint8Array, pageNum: number) {
  const pdf = await pdfjsLib.getDocument({ data: pdfBytes }).promise;
  const page = await pdf.getPage(pageNum);

  const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale: 1.5 });
  canvas.height = viewport.height;
  canvas.width = viewport.width;

  await page.render({ canvasContext: context, viewport }).promise;
}
```

### 5. AI Assistant Rules

#### OpenAI Integration (Main Process)

```javascript
ipcMain.handle("ask-ai", async (event, prompt) => {
  const fetch = (await import("node-fetch")).default;

  const response = await fetch("https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY}`,
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      model: "gpt-4o-mini",
      messages: [
        { role: "system", content: "You are a helpful assistant..." },
        { role: "user", content: prompt },
      ],
      temperature: 0.2,
    }),
  });

  const data = await response.json();
  return { success: true, content: data.choices[0].message.content };
});
```

### 6. Security & Performance Rules

#### Electron Security

```javascript
// Main window security
new BrowserWindow({
  webPreferences: {
    nodeIntegration: false, // Disable Node.js in renderer
    contextIsolation: true, // Isolate context
    enableRemoteModule: false, // Disable remote module
    preload: path.join(__dirname, "preload.js"),
  },
});

// Prevent new window creation
app.on("web-contents-created", (event, contents) => {
  contents.on("new-window", (event, navigationUrl) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    // Handle in current browser view instead
  });
});
```

#### Performance Optimization

- **Lazy Loading**: Load PDF.js worker only when needed
- **Memory Management**: Clear PDF data when switching tabs
- **Event Cleanup**: Remove all listeners in useEffect cleanup
- **Debounced Updates**: Use debouncing for resize events

### 7. Development Workflow

#### Project Structure

```
myai-pdf-electron/
├── main.js              # Electron main process
├── preload.js            # IPC bridge
├── package.json          # Main dependencies
├── frontend/             # React application
│   ├── src/App.tsx      # Main React component
